    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0073" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Woodrow Wilson Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lloyd
                        George</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-14">14 November,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>May I not express my sincere admiration of the admirable temper and purpose of
                    your address of the eleventh [<hi rendition="#italic">twelfth</hi>] just
                    reproduced <pb facs="0074" n="4" xml:id="pg4"/> in part in our papers.<anchor
                        n="3a" xml:id="d8-f1"/> It is delightful to be made aware of such community
                    of thought and counsel in approaching the high and difficult task now awaiting
                    us.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d8-f1" n="3a" xml:id="d8-f1-content">
                <p>Full text printed in the London <hi rendition="#italic">Times</hi>, Nov. 13,
                    1918, p. 9.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
